# ─── Solo Dev Vibecoding Notes ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is a locally-hosted app built solo with AI-assisted development.
# Here's how the workflow is set up:
#
# Git strategy:
#   - main is always deployable — branch off, squash-merge back, delete
#   - Commit messy on feature branches (it's your undo history)
#   - Tag milestones: git tag v0.1-auth-working
#   - Don't bikeshed branch names or commit messages pre-squash
#
# Testing philosophy (80/20 rule):
#   - tsc + vite build + unit tests on tricky logic = 80% safety for 5% effort
#   - Write tests when bugs bite you, not for everything
#   - Skip E2E early — slow, brittle, overkill for solo dev
#   - Regression tests grow organically: bug appears → test first → fix
#
# Local workflow:
#   - npm run test:watch     → vitest watch mode (fast feedback while coding)
#   - npm run validate       → full lint+typecheck+build+test before merge
#   - Pre-commit hook runs validate automatically
#   - npm run test           → quick frontend+backend tests
#
# CI (GitHub Actions):
#   - validate.yml           → lint, typecheck, build, test (frontend+backend)
#   - container-sanity.yml   → Docker build + health check
#   - docker-publish.yml     → GHCR publish on main/tags
#
# Process exists to protect you from yourself:
#   - Roll back mistakes quickly (squash-merged PRs + tags)
#   - Understand what you did in 2 weeks (PR descriptions + clean main)
#   - Not lose work (commit often, push often)
#   - Skip anything that doesn't serve those three goals
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
